<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The second is Tyler Stalman&#8217;s <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Zt-fS0DH8BQ">iPhone 18 Pro &amp; Duo: A Photographer&#8217;s Reaction</a>. Tyler set me straight on the variable aperture. The mechanism isn&#8217;t there to create more bokeh. At its widest setting, the lens is already as open as it gets. The clever bit is that Apple can put a faster lens in the phone, then stop it down when conditions call for less light or more depth of field.</p>



